adjudication.rationale:
The diff adds `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts` with an auth check:

```ts
if (req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
  return res.status(403)
}
```

If `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is **unset** (i.e., `undefined`), and the request also omits that header (so `req.headers[...]` is `undefined`), the condition becomes `undefined !== undefined` which is `false`, so the request is **not rejected**. That is a fail-open authentication bug that is directly verifiable from the code.

Additionally, the handler has no `req.method` guard, and after passing the above check it performs DB writes (`credential.update/create`) based solely on `userId` and `appSlug` from the request body (no session/ownership check). The timing-safe comparison point is accurate (plain `!==`). The only speculative part is whether `APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED` is always false in practice; that constant’s value isn’t in the diff, but the fail-open logic itself is a real defect when the endpoint is reachable.
